# Line endings.
#
# Source is normalised to LF on commit. Without this, a commit made on Windows
# rewrites a whole file's line endings and the real change disappears into a
# thousand-line diff — main's #81 showed 2,396 changed lines for what was
# actually 83 insertions, because it also flipped index.css and
# ProductDetailPage.jsx from CRLF to LF.
#
# Scoped to the types the app owns rather than a blanket `* text=auto`:
# .dockerignore, .env.example, package.json and package-lock.json are CRLF in
# the index today, and a blanket rule would renormalise them — a 20k-line
# package-lock diff — the next time anyone touched them. Add them here only
# alongside a deliberate renormalisation commit.
*.ts    text eol=lf
*.tsx   text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf

# Playwright baselines are byte-compared; never let git touch them.
*.png   binary
*.woff2 binary
